
TODO / bugs / feature ideas, in order of importance:

* Build improvements - bump RmlUI to latest and make sure it's statically linked. We want to be able to bundle it with BitRiot so people can play without needing to download separate deps. SDL 2.x can stay dynamic as it's a very common dependency to have installed.

* Scoreboard: End game "Scoreboard" should be cleaned up a bit - how about stats for all players in a column format, and a smaller font?

* AI: boxed-in bot livelock. A bot walled in by blocks that has its own eggs and creatures on its tile can stay stuck forever and never lays the bomb that would free it. Repro: `BITRIOT_TEST_SEED=6 ./build/tests/bitriot_tests --gtest_filter='AISeekEnergyTest.HealthyBotWithAnEggUnderItselfStillGetsOutToAPickupInTime'` (stuck at (1,1); a frame trace shows 0 bombs, and its health climbing on self-made energy drops). Pre-existing, not caused by the seeded RNG: that one test fails about 0.075% of seeds on `claude` with libc rand (e.g. 3294, 5845, 6821). Suspected cause, NOT root-caused: the chain-blast rule in `safeLocationToBomb`/`bombSiteAcceptable` refuses a bomb site with an egg on or beside it, and the bot keeps laying new eggs on its own tile. Look at whether a boxed-in bot should stop laying eggs, or bomb anyway when it can survive.

* Rules: co-op stalemate - a round can still never end. Seen at full-suite BITRIOT_TEST_SEED=276 (FullRoundTest.ThreeConsecutiveCoopRoundsAllComplete, round 3): the last AI player is on ~7 health, every energy drop is walled off by blocks it can't afford to bomb (and it is too hurt to lay eggs), and the last hostile robot can't reach it or be reached, so nobody ever dies. Not an AI bug - fix/ai-seek-energy covers the cases a bot can get out of - but a rules gap. Options: a stalemate timeout (end the round when the spawner is spent and no health/position changes for N ticks), a "sudden death" phase that slowly drains everyone or shrinks the arena, or leave it as a rare edge case. Must be tick-based so it stays deterministic for netplay.


DONE, but needs verification:

* Bug: Possibly related to playing multiple games (needs further debugging): spinning energy 'rockets' were frequently just shooting "randomly" and not at any targets.
** THIS HAS BEEN FIXED. Regression-guarded by EntitySimTest.AIGameViewIsClearedWhenANewRoundStarts.

* Teams: Team scoreboard does not align very well - text needs to be centred and column headings should be made.
** FIXED in 18eb5ea - reworked into a centred table with a header row and shared column widths.
** VERIFIED by ScoreboardLayoutTest: loads the real scoreboard.rml/.rcss through RmlUi and asserts on computed geometry. Reverting the assets to e28cbf3 fails 7 of its 8 cases. NOTE: this verifies geometry (columns align to within 1px, no overlap, no wrapping), not how it looks.

* Teams: Co-op play never ends - tested a 4 player coop team game and the NPC spawner eventually stopped spawning eggs but the game never ended.
** FIXED in 18eb5ea - a co-op round now also ends when the board is clear of hostile NPCs and the spawning pool is out of points. Covered by WinConditionTest and RoundLifecycleTest.
** VERIFIED by FullRoundTest: plays whole 2- and 4-player co-op rounds to their natural end. Restoring the old co-op branch reproduces the bug exactly - 60000 frames with hostilesRemain=false, poolSpent=true, players alive, round never ends.
** Note: with the NPC Spawner option turned off, a co-op round still never ends. That is deliberate - no enemies can ever spawn, so it is an enemy-free sandbox. Ending it automatically would end it at kickoff.

DONE and verified:

* Player select menu: 'Selected' highlighting of selected items on menu don't show up very well and don't show at all when highlighting portrait images of players on 'Player Select' menu. e.g. of player 1 character doesn't show blue border so it is hard to tell where your input focus is.

* Menu: Menu navigation is not great - 'Start' should be renamed to 'Play' and instead go to the 'Player Select' menu, and 'Player Select' should not show on mainmenu.rml at all.

* Teams: Team play should be implemented - allow team selection on player select menu - if players are on the same team, then they work together and can win together. Spinning energy 'rockets' should not target each other or pteam players' spawn, and they can pass by each other and their spawn without damage plus their spawn do not target or hurt each other. Scoreboard will need updating to reflect stats for each player on the team.

